org/patch/9206519/) Signed-off-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54090 TEST=build and boot on elm  Change-Id: Iebba3674b2265c195d3b709c77e197a81e5be81d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350632 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="350632" owner_email="yong.mao@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/32/350632/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3c630be73e4833131802865d1a020f55e870e9eb" commit="42834d2d8f5339c78809bef2bc90b268ea67554b" commit_message="FROMLIST: mmc: mediatek: fix CRC error when calling mmc_select_hs400()  the tune result of hs200 mode at 200Mhz is not suitable for 50Mhz, mmc_select_hs400() will set clock frequency to 50Mhz, use defalut tune setting for 50Mhz to avoid CRC error.  Signed-off-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9206515/) Signed-off-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54090 TEST=build and boot on elm  Change-Id: I3c630be73e4833131802865d1a020f55e870e9eb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/350680 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="350680" owner_email="yong.mao@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/80/350680/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I08fd01607f8f4cac55b42e5516d239a7d0fb6274" commit="4c5cf9b7a955302b518ddb0c8465d0df39c83f34" commit_message="FROMLIST: mmc: mediatek: fix CMD21/CMD19 timeout issue  we did not deal with the read data of CMD21/CMD19 if there is response CRC error of CMD21/CMD19, in this case, eMMC/SD may still in send-data state. therefore, all of next commands cannot get response as device is not in transfer state.  for resolving this issue, still need deal with the data receive to make device back to transfer state.  Signed-off-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9206441/) Signed-off-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54090 TEST=build and boot on elm  Change-Id: I08fd01607f8f4cac55b42e5516d239a7d0fb6274 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354890 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354890" owner_email="yong.mao@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/90/354890/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6d60c7839717a485fbe744dd6500041cbdcebfd6" commit="bb30ffdda6b8267d9e104059430018d361952cba" commit_message="alsa_api_test: Check device consumption rate  The sleep time in each period might not be accurate. Check device consumption rate rather than checking buffer level.  BUG=chromium:617516 TEST=run alsa_api_test --move on samus.  Change-Id: I6d60c7839717a485fbe744dd6500041cbdcebfd6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357691 C